The repository’s current hardener explicitly treats empty length-limited HTTP-200 replies as failed attempts and currently uses a two-model pool; the README discloses that limitation. I’m now rerunning the full local self-test, including the measured 276.8-million-operation reference sweep, to verify the saved report from scratch.
